outputs.exact_statement:
For distinct unassigned indices $i,j$, $$\label{eq:coefficientpair}
 4c^{\sigma}_{ij}c^{\sigma}_{ji}\le z_{\sigma}^2.$$ For distinct unassigned indices $i,j,k$, $$\label{eq:coefficient}
 c^{\sigma}_{ij}c^{\sigma}_{jk}\le z_{\sigma}c^{\sigma}_{ik}.$$

With the notation above, $$\label{eq:transport}
 (\overline H_p-\overline H_d)^2
 \le
 \left(\frac1{s_pW_p}+\frac1{s_dW_d}
       +\frac2{s_ps_d}\sum_{t=1}^m\frac{v_t}{W_t}\right)
 D_{\mathcal X}(H).$$

For good multipliers and every $H:\Omega\to\mathbb R$, $$\label{eq:transversalvariance}
 \operatorname{Var}_\mu H\le C_{\rm p}\frac{D(H)}{c_0},
 \qquad C_{\rm p}=n(1+8n).$$

Assume the multipliers are good, and let $H:\Omega\to\mathbb R$. For each defect type $ij$ there is an event $\mathcal A\subseteq\Omega_0$ obtained by prescribing the selected elements in pairs $i,j$, with $\mu(\mathcal A)\ge1/4$. Its conditional mean $\overline H'=\mathbb E_\mu[H\mid\mathcal A]$ satisfies $$\label{eq:defecttransfer}
 (\overline H_{ij}-\overline H')^2
       \le C_{\rm d}\frac{D(H)}{c_0},
 \qquad C_{\rm d}=8+32n,$$ and $$\label{eq:conditionalmean}
 (\overline H'-\overline H_0)^2\le4\operatorname{Var}_\mu H.$$

For good multipliers and every $H:\Omega\to\mathbb R$, $$\label{eq:observable}
 \operatorname{Var}_\pi(\mathsf QH)\le K_{\rm obs}\mathcal E(H),
 \qquad K_{\rm obs}=2000n^6.$$

Suppose the multipliers are good. If $G=\mathsf QG$ and a trajectory $(X_t)$ of $P$ starts with law $\nu\le U\pi$, then for every integer $N\ge1$, $$\label{eq:MSE}
 \mathbb E_\nu\left[\left(\frac1N\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}G(X_t)-\mathbb E_\pi G\right)^2\right]
 \le\frac{2UK_{\rm obs}\operatorname{Var}_\pi G}{N}.$$

With good multipliers, $P_A$ is reversible with stationary law $\mu$, irreducible, and lazy. Its inverse spectral gap is at most $18n^4$. In particular, for every integer $s\ge0$, $$\label{eq:tracemixing}
 \left|\frac{P_A^s(x,y)}{\mu(y)}-1\right|
 \le\frac{\exp(-s/(18n^4))}{\min_{z\in A}\mu(z)}
 \quad(x,y\in A).$$ If a trace step begins with a law $\nu\le U\mu$, its expected number of underlying transitions is at most $$\label{eq:returncost}
 \frac{U}{\pi(A)}\le5Un^2.$$
